<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "The Connect window is where you sign in. It opens over the chat at its own address, /connect — from Create an account on the home, or from anything you try that needs an account — so you sign in without leaving the desktop you arrived on."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_status_user}>{dgettext("help", "Signing In")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "Type a nickname and click Continue. A nickname nobody has registered opens a short registration form; a registered one asks for its password. Either way you land in the chat already identified."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext("help", "The nickname rules are the same everywhere — see")}
  <.help_link topic="connecting">{dgettext("help", "Connecting")}</.help_link>
  {dgettext("help", "for the full list.")}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_devices}>{dgettext("help", "Trusted Terminals")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "Tick Remember this terminal when you log in, and this browser remembers your nickname. Next time, the window lists your nicknames instead of an empty field. Click Log in beside one and you are in, without a password."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "Log in with another nickname opens an empty field, and Back to the list goes back."
  )}
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "What each terminal is — its browser, its system, when it was last used — is in Trusted Terminals, in the Start menu."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_connect}>{dgettext("help", "Auto-Login")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "A remembered terminal can go one step further: turn on auto-login for it and opening any page signs you straight into the chat, with nothing to click."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "Auto-login is set per terminal and per nickname, so a shared computer can stay manual."
  )}
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "After you disconnect, or when a session ends, this window opens instead of the chat. Auto-login starts again when you close the browser, or when you log in here."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_laptop}>{dgettext("help", "The Window Itself")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help",
    "It behaves like every other window: move it, minimize it, or bring it back from its taskbar button. Closing it takes you back to the chat; after signing in you land where you were going — the channel you were reading, or the game or call that asked you to sign in."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="connecting">{dgettext("help", "Connecting")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="connect-authentication">
    {dgettext("help", "Connect Authentication")}
  </.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="ui-desktop">{dgettext("help", "Desktop & Windows")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="nickserv">{dgettext("help", "NickServ Overview")}</.help_link>
</p>
